      "@id": "#claim",
      "@type": "Claim",
      "name": "Entry 9: closed-form models vs the Pedal Hidrográfico urban rides",
      "text": "All three models reproduce measured energy to ~4–7% median with a generic assumed rider (poor-man's ε=0.20 best at 3.9%); ε_geom over-credits descent recovery on stop-go riding — the braking penalty the open rural rides could not isolate — giving the corpus rule: ε_geom on open coastable routes, flat ε ≈ 0.20 on urban stop-go; a physical-plausibility floor excluded 7 rides whose energy deficit is a power-channel problem, not walking.",
      "appearance": [
        {
          "@id": "https://github.com/danlessa/bicycling-energy-model/blob/main/research/journal/MODEL_COMPARISON_JOURNAL.md"
        }
      ],
